                <head>Annex A</head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Classification of UN Members in Terms of the
                        Viewpoint Normally Taken by Them on Colonial Questions in UN Bodies</hi>
                </p>
                <p>It is recognized that numerous exceptions could be found to the following
                    classification and that many variations of viewpoint exist among the UN Members
                    listed in each category; however, it is believed that on the basis of past
                    performance the following classification is a useful indication of the way in
                    which Members of the UN are likely to be grouped on colonial questions arising
                    in UN bodies.</p>
                <table cols="5" rows="24">
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">Conservative Colonial Viewpoint</hi></cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">Moderate Colonial Viewpoint</hi></cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">States Having Sympathy with Colonial
                                Group</hi></cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">Moderate Anti-Colonial Viewpoint</hi></cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">Extreme Anti-Colonial Viewpoint</hi></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
